        "title": "iPhone Ultra is coming, but it might not have these key features",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/24/iphone-ultra-wont-have-these-five-features/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/03/iphone-fold-mockup-purple.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple’s first foldable iPhone will reportedly be announced in just over two weeks. Despite potentially being branded as the “<a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/11/everyone-at-apple-uses-iphone-ultra-name-says-mark-gurman/\">iPhone Ultra</a>” and <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/24/iphone-ultra-is-coming-six-new-features-in-apples-top-tier-model/\">priced</a> at over $2,000, it will have several big limitations.</p>",
