        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/03/iphone-fold-mockup-blue.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sometimes a headline is the complete inverse of the real news in the story, and that’s the case with a new survey measuring interest in the upcoming <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/iphone-ultra/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">iPhone Ultra</a>. The headline says 75% of US adults aren’t interested in a folding iPhone, while the real surprise is that as many as 25% are.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/aapl/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Apple</a> shouldn’t get too excited by the results, however, as willingness to pay was way, <em>way</em> less than the price we’re expecting the company to announce …</p>",
